<!DOCTYPE Bill PUBLIC "-//LSC//DTD Authoring Bill XML//EN" "l:\dtd\author\billauthoring.top"><Bill version="1.0" type="introLN" docName="H-4567.1"><IntroducedBillHeader><RequestNumber>H-4567.1</RequestNumber><BillNumber>HOUSE BILL 3190</BillNumber><StateLegSession><State>State of Washington</State><Legislature>58th Legislature</Legislature><Session>2004 Regular Session</Session></StateLegSession><Sponsors>Representative Clements</Sponsors><IntroHistory><ReadDate>Read first time 02/06/2004.  </ReadDate><ReferredTo>Referred to Committee on Transportation.</ReferredTo></IntroHistory></IntroducedBillHeader><BriefDescription>Restricting use of adjustable suspensions.</BriefDescription><BillBody><BillTitle><LineNumber line=" 1" page="1,1" hrt="no"/>	AN ACT Relating to operating motor vehicles with adjustable<LineNumber line=" 2" page="1,2"/>suspensions; and adding a new section to chapter 46.61 RCW.</BillTitle><EnactingClause><LineNumber line=" 3" page="1,3" hrt="no"/>BE IT ENACTED BY THE LEGISLATURE OF THE STATE OF WASHINGTON:</EnactingClause><BillSection type="new" clausetype="newsinglesectoch"><LineNumber line=" 4" page="1,4" hrt="no"/><BegSecNew><NewSecText>NEW SECTION.</NewSecText><SecNum>Sec. </SecNum><BegSecText>A new section is added to chapter <NewSingleSecToCh>46.61</NewSingleSecToCh> RCW<LineNumber line=" 5" page="1,5"/>to read as follows:</BegSecText><LineNumber line=" 6" page="1,6" hrt="no"/></BegSecNew><RCWSLText>	A person shall not raise or lower the height of a motor vehicle by<LineNumber line=" 7" page="1,7"/>mechanical means while the motor vehicle is moving on a highway at a<LineNumber line=" 8" page="1,8"/>speed in excess of fifteen miles per hour.</RCWSLText></BillSection><BillEnd>--- END ---<PageNumberFooter lastpage="yes">		p. 1	HB 3190</PageNumberFooter></BillEnd></BillBody></Bill>